---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout title="Reconnaissance">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-12 px-6">
        
        <a href="/learn" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline mb-8 block font-medium">← Back to Learning Path</a>

        <article class="prose prose-slate lg:prose-lg">
            
            <h1>Reconnaissance: The Art of Discovery</h1>
            <p class="lead">
                Before you attack, you must see. Reconnaissance is the phase of gathering information about your target to find weak spots.
            </p>

            <hr />

            <h2>1. Passive Recon (Google Dorking)</h2>
            <p>
                Gathering info <strong>without touching the target's server</strong> directly.
            </p>
            
            <div class="bg-slate-800 text-slate-200 p-4 rounded-lg font-mono text-sm not-prose mb-6 shadow-lg border border-slate-700">
                <p class="text-green-400 mb-2">// Find exposed configuration files</p>
                <span class="text-purple-400">site:</span>target.com <span class="text-purple-400">ext:</span>env OR <span class="text-purple-400">ext:</span>yaml
                <br><br>
                <p class="text-green-400 mb-2">// Find hidden admin panels</p>
                <span class="text-purple-400">site:</span>target.com <span class="text-purple-400">inurl:</span>admin
            </div>

            <h2>2. Active Recon (Subdomain Enumeration)</h2>
            <p>
                Finding subdomains expands your attack surface. We use tools to query DNS records and find hidden assets.
            </p>

            <div class="my-8 not-prose">
                <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden bg-slate-900 shadow-2xl border border-slate-700">
                    <div class="bg-slate-800 p-3 flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-slate-700">
                        <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500 hover:bg-red-600"></div>
                        <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500 hover:bg-yellow-600"></div>
                        <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500 hover:bg-green-600"></div>
                        <div class="ml-4 text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono">root@kali: ~/recon</div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="p-6 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto">
                        <div class="flex gap-2 mb-4">
                            <span class="text-green-400 font-bold">root@kali:~$</span>
                            <span class="text-white">subfinder -d tesla.com -silent</span>
                        </div>

                        <div class="text-slate-300 space-y-1">
                            <p>auth.tesla.com</p>
                            <p>www.tesla.com</p>
                            <p>shop.tesla.com</p>
                            <p class="text-blue-400">api-staging.tesla.com <span class="text-slate-500 ml-2">// Interesting!</span></p>
                            <p>vpn.tesla.com</p>
                            <p>dev-portal.tesla.com</p>
                            <p>mail.tesla.com</p>
                            <p class="animate-pulse text-green-400 mt-2">... Found 142 subdomains in 4 seconds</p>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div class="flex gap-2 mt-4">
                            <span class="text-green-400 font-bold">root@kali:~$</span>
                            <span class="w-2 h-4 bg-slate-500 animate-pulse"></span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p class="text-center text-sm text-slate-500 mt-3 italic">Figure 1: Simulated output of Subfinder tool.</p>
            </div>

            <h3>Essential Tools</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Subfinder:</strong> Fast passive subdomain enumeration.</li>
                <li><strong>Httpx:</strong> To check which subdomains are alive.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-500 p-4 not-prose mt-8">
                <p class="font-bold text-blue-900">💡 Pro Tip</p>
                <p class="text-blue-800">
                    Always look for <code>staging</code> or <code>dev</code> subdomains. They often have weaker security controls and debug modes enabled.
                </p>
            </div>

        </article>

    </div>
</MainLayout>